# pcbqa self-test evidence

Replaces a stale log that recorded a 43-test run from a much earlier state of
this framework. That log had been sitting in the repository describing a suite
that no longer existed, which is worse than having no log: it answered the
question "is this tested?" with a number roughly a quarter of the real one.

## The run

    command      "C:/Program Files/KiCad/10.0/bin/python.exe" verification/run.py selftest --jobs 6
    working dir  verification/
    started      2026-08-05T08:03:38Z
    interpreter  KiCad 10.0 bundled Python 3.11.5

    tests discovered   172
    passed             171
    skipped              1
    failed               0
    errored              0
    worker processes     6
    elapsed            1054.7 s
    exit code            0

The single skip is
`tests.test_mutations_checks.FixtureInventory.test_a_symlink_in_place_of_a_file_fails`,
which needs the Windows privilege to create a symbolic link and skips itself
rather than reporting a pass it did not earn.

    worker 0: 14 tests, 598.4s of test time
    worker 1: 13 tests, 373.0s of test time
    worker 2: 13 tests, 497.5s of test time
    worker 3: 38 tests, 491.5s of test time
    worker 4: 56 tests, 379.8s of test time
    worker 5: 38 tests, 503.7s of test time

Per-worker test time sums to more than the elapsed wall clock because the
runner distributes individual test IDs, so a class fixture runs once per test
method rather than once per class. That is the cost of every test being
independently addressable and sharing no state.

## What was tested

    HEAD at run time   1538e6c500d4c39395f3feb0a9528e7a505d02fa
    tree digest        e5d31597006e8ce5d3467e670457ab184d933cf1d6b39d0e83a2c3fb69e70bb4

`tree digest` is a sha256 over every tracked file under `verification/` -
each file's path, then the sha256 of its bytes, in sorted path order, across
137 files. It identifies the source that actually ran, which a commit hash
alone cannot do while changes are staged.

The working tree at run time carried the staged-but-uncommitted changes of the
pass that produced this file: the portability fixture restored to its content
at 71cf337, `verification/out` removed from the index, and that pass's source
changes. If those are committed unchanged, the tree digest above still
identifies exactly what ran; only the HEAD line becomes stale.

## Reproducing

    cd verification
    "C:/Program Files/KiCad/10.0/bin/python.exe" run.py preflight
    "C:/Program Files/KiCad/10.0/bin/python.exe" run.py selftest --jobs 6

`--jobs 1` runs the same tests serially and is the slower control; the runner
asserts in `tests/test_runner.py` that both execute the same test IDs. Output
goes to `verification/out/`, which is generated and git-ignored.
